        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "009d9c3d-c7ee-50f2-abb0-efc7f74d7de8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pravda, Stiffelio, Aroldo\n- People: Giuseppe Verdi, Francesco Maria Piave, Lajos Magyar\n- Organizations: Communist Party of the Soviet Union, Comintern\n- Places: Soviet Union\n\nFacts:\n- In 1850, Giuseppe Verdi and Francesco Maria Piave collaborated on the opera \"Stiffelio,\" which has three acts and an Italian libretto by Piave.\n- Aroldo is a four-act opera by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto by Francesco Maria Piave, and it was based on and adapted from their earlier collaboration \"Stiffelio.\"\n- In 1922, Lajos Magyar went to the Soviet Union in a prisoner exchange.\n- In the Soviet Union, Lajos Magyar worked on the staff of the Comintern and at the newspaper Pravda.\n- Pravda is a Russian broadsheet newspaper.\n- Pravda was formerly the official newspaper of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union.\n- While it was the official newspaper of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union, Pravda was one of the most influential papers in the country and had a circulation of 11 million.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2075c5d2-ba5e-524b-87d3-ba73bc3117e9",
        "text": "Page: Pravda. Sentence: Pravda (Russian: Правда ; ] , \"Truth\") is a Russian broadsheet newspaper, formerly the official newspaper of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union, when it was one of the most influential papers in the country with a circulation of 11 million.\nPage: Stiffelio. Sentence: Stiffelio is an opera in three acts by Giuseppe Verdi, from an Italian libretto by Francesco Maria Piave.\nPage: Lajos Magyar. Sentence: In 1922 Magyar went to the Soviet Union as the result of an exchange of prisoners; there he worked on the staff of the Comintern and at the newspaper Pravda.\nPage: Aroldo. Sentence: Aroldo (] ) is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi to an Italian libretto by Francesco Maria Piave, based on and adapted from their earlier 1850 collaboration, \"Stiffelio\".",
